 partial\n   equilibrium, not a solver bug); clean-HEAD VK attribution matches the\n   candidate exactly; pre-yield controls (direct/interp elastic == plastic,\n   alpha_max = 0); serialized Q4 checkpoint limitation documented\n   (pre-existing, out of repair scope).\n\n## Completed in this continuation run (source/test/harness edits)\n\n1. Harness v2 (exception-proof try/finally accounting, --src-override exact\n   import routing with recorded import-origin check, named pytest count\n   parsing, per-input hashing, JIT/thread preflight record). Supervisor\n   follow-up applied: active-phase start/completion tracking so a\n   harness-side exception after launch charges the child's elapsed time\n   after owned-process cleanup (phase_start cleared at each phase end).\n2. ep_attribution.py prose corrected to the adopted partial-equilibrium\n   decision.\n3. Source repairs in the two owned files:\n   - R1 corotational.py: fail-closed guard refusing downstream non-support\n     equations that use a rotating slave translation as a nonzero master\n     (normalized compiler equations; rotation covectors, upstream shell\n     ties and linear-only chains preserved).\n   - R3 nonlinear_static.py n_red==0 selector: corrected after supervisor\n     recheck. checkpoint_resume/force_restart use the already mapped\n     initial_committed_displacement; every fresh path expands raw u0\n     through the map exactly once (fresh force control commits T@q which\n     is zero at n_red==0 and would discard prescribed master motion).\n   - R4 nonlinear_static.py: rotating-MPC auto resolves work_conjugate\n     even with follower loads; explicit rotated/consistent refused on the\n     new route; follower NotImplementedError exempts the resolved\n     work_conjugate route.\n   - R5 nonlinear_static.py: DC admission uses full_u(q) at the actual\n     initial state for both the control row (map Jacobian) and\n     proportional-load reduction; linear admission retained when the map\n     is absent; proportional load reduction also evaluated at full_u(q).\n4. tests/test_nonlinear_beam_shell_slice3.py (new, LF): R1 (4 cases),\n   R2 guard (initial fields + corotational refused), R3 (direct/interp\n   prescribed rigid rotation; builder root_supports=False for the\n   prescribed-motion fixture; asserts prescribed shell values AND beam\n   lever arm AND strain-free mapped state), R4 (auto+follower dispatch,\n   pressure->0 continuity, legacy refusal on route, legacy retention off\n   route, complete reduced derivative vs central FD, external-only\n   derivative J^T K_ext J + geometric_tangent(u,F_ext) vs FD on its own\n   scale), R5 (zero-rotation refusal; finite-state admission via genuine\n   pre-solve restart).\n\n## Remaining (in execution order)\n\n1. Run the repairs module under the harness in -k batches; fix failures.\n2. Write tests/test_nonlinear_beam_shell_slice3_continuation.py: EP DC\n   direct/interp continuation (half 6 -> -0.10, resume 6 -> -0.20 with deep\n   copied initial_displacements/initial_element_states,\n   equilibrate_initial_state=False, emit_restart_checkpoint=False;\n   uninterrupted 12 -> -0.20), independent residual at actual\n   result.load_factor (<=1e-7), control target <=1e-8 m, positive plastic\n   strain, constraints, force/wrench reactions, input immutability\n   (successful resume, rejected resume, cancellation; then clean reuse),\n   rejected-step snapshots exclude rejected history, cancellation via\n   progress_callback. Module-level solve cache shared with the final\n   regression.\n3. Mesh study script (new diagnostics/mesh_study.py; R1-R4 @12k, M1-M4/\n   P1-P4 @140k + corresponding linear; gates from the assignment; per-case\n   flush).\n4. Arc reference: analytical_derivation.md (adopted supervisor formulas) +\n   diagnostics/arc_reference.py; constrained plane-section rows, nx 8/16/32\n   x ny2, e 0/0.002, 30/60 deg, matching and 1.5nx nonmatching; 1%/0.25%\n   gates; refinements 64/128/256 only if authorized conditions hold.\n5. Final regression: 25 historical + 2 Slice1/2 + new Slice3 modules via\n   scripts/run_portable_ci.py --development, one thread, JIT off, no\n   retired imports; 600 s cap may use --allow-reserve.\n6. HANDOVER active section 8 update + concise final handoff.\n\n## Reserved decisions (for Astra)\n\n- Arc-reference refinements beyond nx32 remain conditional on the\n  supervisor's prospective authorization (errors decreasing, budget).\n- No physics, tolerance or public-contract changes have been made; any\n  such finding will be reported as a proposal.\n", "numLines": 94, "startLine": 1, "requestedOffset": null, "requestedLimit": 2000, "totalLines": null, "wasTruncated": false}, "outputText": "", "durationMs": 0.0, "display": {"success": true, "verb": "Read", "message": "94 lines from C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\.development\\nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\\checkpoint.md", "warnings": [], "approvalNote": null, "suffix": ""}, "decision": "execute", "approvalType": "always", "approvalSource": "bypass"}}
