\nCould this be the PLASTICITY? eps_p 8e-3 at failure point for interp, 2e-2 for direct. The S355 curve: eps_p_y1, eps_p_y2 — the hardening curve has a knee; at some plastic strain the return mapping might oscillate (numerical non-convergence of the constitutive return at the material level) — but that would show as residual stagnation.\n\nLet me think about the residual trajectory: if Newton is converging quadratically, 40 iterations is a LOT — any healthy step converges in <10. A stall means the tangent is inconsistent with the residual at the current state. The work_conjugate tangent for the rotating map: K_red = J^T(K_T - K_ext)J + K_mpc,geom(u, f_int - f_ext). The geometric term uses the IMBALANCE f_b at the slave. During Newton iterations the imbalance → 0, so K_geom → 0 at convergence — consistent tangent ✓ in theory.\n\nHmm wait — but actually, is the issue the SHELL corotational tangent itself (not the map)? The shell element corotational \"work_conjugate\" tangent... The R4 test verified the complete reduced derivative matches FD to 1e-6 at a moderate random state (rotations up to 0.35 rad). So the tangent IS consistent (FD-verified). Then Newton should converge quadratically... unless the FD test state didn't exercise the plastic return-mapping tangent (the R4 test used elastic states? _assemble_nonlinear_system with states {} — EMPTY states → elastic! The FD test verified the elastic tangent, not the plastic one!).\n\nSo a plausible defect: the plastic consistent tangent (or its interaction with the rotating map) is inconsistent at larger plastic strains → Newton stalls. But wait — the plasticity tangent is the element's dP/deps (algorithmic tangent) — used in both rotated and work_conjugate routes equally. The half run to -0.10 (eps_p 1.2e-2) converged fine with 7 iterations/step. Step 11 (eps_p → 2.4e-2) stalls. Hmm.\n\nActually — hold on, let me reconsider. Maybe it's not a stall: maybe Newton DIVERGES (residual grows) and the cutback mechanism kicks in but... failure_reason \"maximum_iterations_reached\" — let me look at the DC failure handling code to understand what happens when max_iterations is hit: does it cutback or stop? Let me read the code after the iteration loop.", "summary": []}
